            <ArticleTitle>Molecular magnesium hydrides supported by an anionic triazacyclononane-type ligand.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1761-1765</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6dt04654a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Molecular magnesium hydride with a terminal metal-hydrogen bond [Mg(iPr2TACN·AliBu3)H]2 supported by a monoanionic TACN-type ligand (TACN = 1,4-di-isopropyl-1,4,7-triazacyclononane) rearranges to form the dinuclear magnesium hydride [Mg(iPr2TACN·AlHiBu2)(μ-H)]2, exhibiting a rare MgH-Al interaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
